    "body": "@DemelzaFeltham `title` on `iframe` can trigger a tooltip popup also but I've only done it when the cursor is on the frame border (worked in Chrome, Firefox, Safari).\n\n@eeeps Navigating through your 'pen using VoiceOver (macOS 15.3.2, Safari 18.3.1) element-by-element (VO+right arrow), I could navigate to the `video` and its name was announced. However, using Read All (VO+A), it stopped at the heading before the video.\n\nI think where `title` fits in the name and description computations is pretty good, if it weren't for the tooltip behavior, it would be easier to advocate for. If authors had a way, likely in CSS, to suggest that user agents not show the tooltip, that would help.   `pointer-events: none` has that effect but as I mentioned, it prevents _all_ pointer interactions on `video` elements (other elements too, like `iframe`). If that property had a more specific value that was effectively `notooltip`, that could do it.",
